<%#
  ONE PANEL'S SLOT (2026-09-09, the page editor; spec §3, §5). The grid item is this div, not the
  panel's own section, so the width class comes from the layout without ten partials learning
  about widths, and so edit mode can hang a control strip and a ghost state on any panel without
  touching what the panel renders.

  THE BODY IS CAPTURED FIRST. Photos and Schematics render NOTHING when they have nothing to show;
  on the normal page an empty slot would still occupy a grid cell, so a blank body renders no slot
  at all — exactly the page before slots existed. In edit mode the same blank body renders a
  PLACEHOLDER instead, because a panel that cannot be seen cannot be arranged.

  THE DATA ATTRIBUTES ARE THE DRAFT. layout_editor_controller.js reads its state off these slots
  and writes changes back to them; there is no second copy of the layout in the page.
  `data-view` is present only for a panel that offers views (Maker::ProjectKind.offered_views).

  Locals: key; extra (passed through to projects/_panel_body).

  EVERY LOCAL IS SPELLED `name: name`, NEVER THE `name:` SHORTHAND, when it is the LAST argument on
  its line. Ruby's value-omitted shorthand keeps looking for a value across the newline, so a render
  ending in a bare `extra:` swallowed the NEXT ERB line — the width assignment below — as that
  argument's value: measured here, the panel body was handed the string "full" as its locals map.
  It fails loudly in this shape and would pass silently in others.

  A TAB KEY IS A SEPARATOR, NOT A PANEL (2026-09-09, tabs), AND ITS BRANCH IS FIRST FOR A REASON:
  everything below asks a question a tab has no answer to — `projects/_panel_body` interpolates the
  key into a partial name (`projects/tab:3f9a…`, missing), and the placeholder asks
  `@panel_labels.fetch(key)`, which raises. It reaches this partial only from the edit-mode loop
  over `order`; the read pages render projects/_panel_groups and never yield a tab key.
%>
<% if @panel_layout.tab?(key) %>
  <%= render "projects/tab_slot", key: key, name: @panel_layout.tab_name_for(key) %>
<% else %>
<% body = render "projects/panel_body", key: key, extra: extra %>
<% width = @panel_layout.width_for(key) %>
<% if @editing %>
  <% hidden = @panel_layout.hidden?(key) %>
  <% offered = Maker::ProjectKind.offered_views(key) %>
  <div class="panel-slot panel--<%= width %><%= " panel-slot--hidden" if hidden %>"
       data-layout-editor-target="slot" data-key="<%= key %>" data-hidden="<%= hidden %>" data-width="<%= width %>"
       <% if offered.any? %>data-view="<%= @panel_layout.view_for(key) %>"<% end %>
       <%# A BLOCK'S CONTENT IS DRAFT STATE LIKE EVERY OTHER FIELD (2026-09-09, content blocks):
           its text, its link and its picture live on the slot, so layout_editor_controller.js still
           reads the whole document off these divs and Save posts one thing. `data-title` and
           `data-intro` stay empty for a block — the strip offers neither, and a link's title is
           `data-link-title`, its own content rather than a panel heading. %>
       <% if (b = @panel_layout.block?(key) && @blocks_by_key[key]) %>
         data-kind="<%= b.kind %>" data-heading="<%= b.heading %>" data-body="<%= b.body %>"
         data-url="<%= b.url %>" data-link-title="<%= b.kind == "link" ? b.heading : "" %>"
         data-line="<%= b.line %>" data-file="<%= b.node_id %>" data-caption="<%= b.caption %>"
       <% end %>
       data-title="<%= @panel_layout.titles[key] %>" data-intro="<%= @panel_layout.intros[key] %>"
       data-always="<%= Maker::ProjectKind::ALWAYS.include?(key) %>">
    <%= render "projects/panel_strip", key: key, hidden: hidden, width: width, offered: offered %>
    <div class="panel-slot-body" data-layout-editor-target="body">
      <% if body.blank? %>
        <section class="panel panel--placeholder">
          <h2><%= @panel_layout.title_for(key, @panel_labels.fetch(key)) %></h2>
          <%# The intro too, where the maker set one, so the placeholder reads like the panel it
              stands in for and the live edit has a line to update rather than one to invent. %>
          <% if (intro = @panel_layout.intro_for(key)) %><p class="panel-intro muted"><%= intro %></p><% end %>
          <p class="muted">Nothing here yet. This panel appears on the page once it has something to show.</p>
        </section>
      <% else %>
        <%= body %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </div>
<% elsif body.present? %>
  <div class="panel-slot panel--<%= width %>"><%= body %></div>
<% end %>
<% end %>
